\section{Caveats}{
\itemize{
\item Maximum likelihood over the cells, each cell's probability integrated over its latent normal by 12-node adaptive Gauss-Hermite quadrature and maximized by Nelder-Mead. mzLib returns the point estimate only: no standard errors.
\item By default the fit is on detection (any success or none), not on how many trials succeeded: on PTM data, mzLib's documentation says, the full counts follow occupancy more weakly and predict covered zeros worse.
\item The link is in natural log-odds and is what stats fit-latent-mixed \code{--link} takes. Which cells enter, and their latent means and SDs, are the caller's modelling choices; the bridge builds neither.
\item With \code{--with-depth} true and no depth column, every cell's depth is 0 and the data say nothing about depth_slope.
}
}
\section{Performance}{
Every call starts one bridge process, which costs a .NET start-up before any work. 
